            "RuntimeException": "- if",
            "task": "itself throws one (rethrown as-is, preserving normal control-flow for callers that distinguish specific unchecked exceptions)"
          }
        }
      ],
      "documentation": "Java method: static runWithTimeout",
      "javadoc_description": "Runs task on a bounded background (daemon) thread, guarding against blocking I/O - typically remote N5/Zarr discovery, that can otherwise hang indefinitely on a stalled connection with no feedback to the user.\n\nUnlike `openRemoteStream(String)` (a single bounded connection), this bounds the *entire* operation, however many network round-trips it internally makes.\n\nOn timeout, the background thread is best-effort interrupted via `ExecutorService.shutdownNow()`; if the underlying I/O call ignores interruption (common for plain socket reads), that thread may still leak until the stalled connection itself eventually times out or errors, but the calling thread is freed immediately to report the failure, rather than hanging alongside it.",
      "category": "Static Methods",
      "deprecated": false,
      "since_version": null,
      "see_also": [],
      "examples": []
    },
